**Goal** — Replace the O(n) full re-import in `RagService.importGraphify()` with an incremental diff-and-apply algorithm against durable `GraphNode`/`GraphLink` Prisma tables.

**Motivation** — `importGraphify()` currently calls `deleteAllBySourceType('code')` then re-indexes all nodes, causing O(n) memory load and no incremental update path.

**Approach** — Compute a diff between the incoming graphify nodes/links and the stored graph in `GraphNode`/`GraphLink` Prisma tables. Apply only the delta (added, modified, removed nodes/links). For removed nodes: delete from both Prisma and LanceDB. For added/updated nodes: upsert into Prisma, regenerate adjacency text only if label/type/sourceFile/outgoing links changed, then upsert into LanceDB. Links: upsert link records, delete stale links. Existing graphify imports remain project-scoped and continue to honor `Project.graphifyEnabled`.

**Scope** — In: `IncrementalGraphDiffService`, `GraphStoreService`, `GraphNode`/`GraphLink` Prisma models, modifying `RagService.importGraphify()` to call `diffAndApply` instead of `deleteAllBySourceType`. CASL extension: `KodaAction.IMPORT`, `'CodeIntel'` subject, factory permission rule. Out: No changes to Phase 2 retrieval scoring, Phase 3 semantic memory, or graphify DTO shape. LanceDB document schema unchanged.

**Interface**
```typescript
class IncrementalGraphDiffService {
  constructor(
    private graphStore: GraphStoreService,
    private rag: RagService,
  ) {}
  async diffAndApply(projectId: string, newNodes: GraphifyNodeDto[], newLinks: GraphifyLinkDto[]): Promise<DiffResult>
  async getStoredGraph(projectId: string): Promise<StoredGraph>
}
interface StoredGraph {
  nodeMap: Map<string, GraphifyNodeDto>;
  linkMap: Map<string, GraphifyLinkDto[]>;
}
interface DiffResult {
  added: number;
  updated: number;
  removed: number;
  indexed: number;
  durationMs: number;
}
```

**Goal** — Introduce a deterministic `AstIndexService` that parses TypeScript/JavaScript source files with `ts-morph` and indexes symbols at the symbol level into the `Symbol` Prisma table.

**Motivation** — Adjacency text from graphify is not true symbol-level metadata; callers and callees cannot be resolved.

**Approach** — Parse TypeScript/JavaScript source files with a deterministic parser (`ts-morph` preferred for TypeScript projects). Index at the symbol level, not file level. Parser output is the source of truth. LLM-assisted extraction may be used later to enrich summaries, but Phase 4 must not depend on an LLM to identify symbol names, locations, signatures, callers, or callees. Process files changed in the commit only (not full repo). `projectId` comes from the `repoId → projectId` mapping. Symbol ID convention: `{repoId}:{filePath}::{SymbolName}` — unique within a project. If overloaded or nested symbols collide, append a stable parser-derived suffix such as `#2`. The `code_commit` outbox handler resolves changed file contents before calling `indexCommit()`; the webhook controller only enqueues commit metadata.

**Scope** — In: `AstIndexService`, `SymbolStore`, `Symbol` Prisma model, `ts-morph` dependency, `code_commit` outbox fan-out handler registration, `CodeIntelController` with `@RequiredPermission([MANAGE, 'AstIndex'])` for direct calls, CASL extension (`'AstIndex'` subject, factory rule). Out: Webhook controller changes (see US-004), LLM-assisted symbol extraction, full-repo indexing, non-TS/JS language support.

**Interface**
```typescript
class AstIndexService {
  constructor(private codeGraph: CodeGraphService, private symbolStore: SymbolStore) {}
  async indexCommit(repoId: string, commitHash: string, files: SourceFile[]): Promise<SymbolIndexResult>
  async getSymbol(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<Symbol | null>
  async getCallers(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<CallerInfo[]>
  async getCallees(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<CalleeInfo[]>
}
interface SymbolIndexResult {
  commitHash: string;
  symbolsIndexed: number;
  filesIndexed: number;
  fileErrors: Array<{ path: string; error: string }>;
  durationMs: number;
}
interface Symbol {
  id: string;
  symbolId: string;
  projectId: string;
  repoId: string;
  commitHash: string;
  name: string;
  kind: 'class' | 'method' | 'function' | 'interface' | 'enum';
  file: string;
  startLine: number;
  endLine: number;
  signature?: string;
  callers: string[];
  callees: string[];
  docComment?: string;
}
```

